__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.DS_Store
.venv/
.coverage
.pytest_cache/
*.sqlite3-shm
*.sqlite3-wal
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.settings.example

# Locally run reports and derived state. `reports/` also holds committed gate
# evidence that ADRs cite, so only the `local/` subtree is ignored: if a path is
# under reports/local/ it is a local run, and if it is anywhere else under
# reports/ it is recorded evidence. Never move committed evidence into local/.
reports/local/

# Scratch workspaces. Durable sqlite state a run needs but no reader does. A
# workspace that IS evidence lives under reports/<phase>/ and is committed
# deliberately; these are not.
work/

# Derived indexes and vector stores. Rebuildable from the records by definition,
# never a source of truth, and never shared across providers or embedding models
# (see AGENTS.md and TECHNICAL_BLUEPRINT.md 12.2.1). Committing one would let a
# stale index outlive the corpus it was built from.
#
# An ADR-0062 vector ARTIFACT is not one of these and is deliberately tracked.
# It is not rebuildable from the records: it required a provider call that is not
# bit-reproducible, which is why TECHNICAL_BLUEPRINT.md:1667-1671 says to store
# the bytes and have a rebuild replay them. That makes it primary evidence of a
# disclosure, closer to an acquisition than to an index, so it lives in
# `vector-artifacts/`. An index built OVER those artifacts is derived and belongs
# to the names below.
*.index.sqlite3
*.derived.sqlite3
vector-store/
vectors/
embeddings/

# LaTeX byproducts of a publication compile. The bundle manifest covers
# paper.tex and paper.pdf; these are incidental and not manifest-hashed.
output/**/*.aux
output/**/*.log
output/**/*.out
